X-WR-CALNAME:Artificial Empathic Technology Calendar
X-WR-CALDESC:Events of the lecture Artificial Empathic Technology
X-WR-TIMEZONE:Europe/Berlin
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:30636431-3263-4537-a233-313262313731
DTSTAMP:20261026T191845Z
DESCRIPTION:Let us examine the distinctions between emotion-adaptive and ar
 tificially empathic technologies\, encompassing their definitions\, applic
 ation domains such as training\, education\, health coaching\, and caregiv
 ing\, as well as the structure of courses and projects.
DTSTART:20261022T080000Z
DTEND:20261022T100000Z
SUMMARY:From Social Computing to Artifically Empathic Technology
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:36383237-6636-4466-b832-303134643065
DTSTAMP:20261026T191845Z
DESCRIPTION:We are exploring the affect trinity\, basic\, dimensional\, app
 raisal\, and constructivist models\, along with the component model and ob
 servable signals\, and their limitations (“no fingerprint”) are considered
  in the analysis.
DTSTART:20261029T090000Z
DTEND:20261029T110000Z
SUMMARY:Affect\, emotion\, mood and other related concepts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:31386532-6361-4137-b365-656535366533
DTSTAMP:20261026T191845Z
DESCRIPTION:Adopting the mindset and approach of an experimental researcher
 : examining the distinction between science and common sense\, progressing
  from observation to hypothesis formulation\, differentiating between corr
 elation and experimentation\, understanding independent and dependent vari
 ables\, utilizing between-subject and within-subject designs\, and address
 ing threats to validity.
DTSTART:20261105T090000Z
DTEND:20261105T110000Z
SUMMARY:Methods I: Thinking like an Experimenter
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:39636130-3366-4539-a632-353435316436
DTSTAMP:20261026T191845Z
DESCRIPTION:Differentiate between cognitive and affective empathy\, compass
 ion\, Theory of Mind (ToM)\, mentalization\, CASA / Media Equation. And wh
 at is the persona effect.
DTSTART:20261112T090000Z
DTEND:20261112T090000Z
SUMMARY:Empathy\, Theory of Mind\, Mentalization
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:65333433-3339-4339-b236-383930306264
DTSTAMP:20261026T191845Z
DESCRIPTION:Exploring OCC appraisal theory\, the OCEAN personality model\, 
 the PAD mood model\, and the decay of emotional intensity. In practice\, w
 e are modeling characters in ALMA Explorer.
DTSTART:20261119T090000Z
DTEND:20261119T110000Z
SUMMARY:Computational Affect + ALMA Explorer (hands-on)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:30383261-6331-4231-a334-343562613937
DTSTAMP:20261026T191845Z
DESCRIPTION:Getting to know the agentic SIA research framework\, Visual Sce
 neMaker. What are scenes\, and what is a sceneflow? Overview of plugins (A
 LMA\, LLM\, ASR\, TTS\, Wizard of Oz)
DTSTART:20261126T090000Z
DTEND:20261126T110000Z
SUMMARY:Interactive Systems + VisualSceneMaker web (hands-on)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:62386661-6232-4139-a233-623961343636
DTSTAMP:20261026T191845Z
DESCRIPTION:Questionnaires and scale quality\, relational measures (felt se
 curity\, perceived responsiveness\, empathic accuracy)\, power and sample 
 size\, pilot study\, preregistration\, research ethics (consent\, data pro
 tection). Also\, VisualSceneMaker StudyMaster.
DTSTART:20261203T090000Z
DTEND:20261203T110000Z
SUMMARY:Methods II: Measurement and Running a Study
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:36356663-6132-4662-b532-313034363061
DTSTAMP:20261026T191845Z
DESCRIPTION:Understanding fundamental human values\, including safety\, aut
 onomy\, and self-respect\, within the framework of goals\, social roles\, 
 and cultural norms. What exactly are display rules? Explore current techno
 logical approaches – for example\, values incorporated during design time 
 (CCVSD)\, as runtime constraints (CARESSES)\, or as runtime objectives (Ar
 tificially Empathic Technology) – and methods to determine whether these v
 alues have been duly respected.
DTSTART:20261210T110000Z
DTEND:20261210T110000Z
SUMMARY:Values and Norms: What an Empathic System Has to Achieve
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:34363936-3131-4732-b036-633435343333
DTSTAMP:20261026T191845Z
DESCRIPTION:Predictive processing\, Moser & von Zeppelin (structural\, situ
 ational\, and communicative emotions)\, self versus display regulation\, M
 ARSSI.
DTSTART:20261217T090000Z
DTEND:20261217T110000Z
SUMMARY:KET I: Regulation and the Individual
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:37313838-3965-4637-b332-336435356264
DTSTAMP:20261026T191845Z
DESCRIPTION:Descriptive statistics\, t-tests\, ANOVA\, effect sizes\, repor
 ting\, open science (p-hacking\, HARKing)
DTSTART:20270107T090000Z
DTEND:20270107T110000Z
SUMMARY:Methods III: Data Analysis
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:63666338-3032-4639-b161-636332613662
DTSTAMP:20261026T191845Z
DESCRIPTION:Person objects and relationships\; inner and outer communicatio
 n paths. Regulation vs. Co-Regulation\, especially repair\, as shown in th
 e context of Mentalization-Based Therapy.
DTSTART:20270114T090000Z
DTEND:20270114T110000Z
SUMMARY:KET II: Relationship and Social Interaction
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:61373162-3663-4231-b438-393931633835
DTSTAMP:20261026T191845Z
DESCRIPTION:Cost function over the value goals\, uncertainty\, explainabili
 ty\, role and limits of LLMs\, deception/dependency\, uncanny valley\, gov
 ernance (EU AI Act\, MEESTAR)\, outlook
DTSTART:20270121T090000Z
DTEND:20270121T110000Z
SUMMARY:KET III: Making Values Computable\, and Limits
END:VEVENT
